2025-05-01 03:10:29 - Thread-1210 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• ball_by_ball."match_id" : groups deliveries that belong to the same match  
• ball_by_ball."over_id", ball_by_ball."ball_id", ball_by_ball."innings_no" : join‑keys that uniquely identify the delivery (used to pair with batsman_scored)  
• ball_by_ball."striker" : the player_id of the batsman who faced the delivery  
• batsman_scored."runs_scored" : runs taken off the bat on that delivery – these are the runs we have to aggregate  
• batsman_scored."match_id", "over_id", "ball_id", "innings_no" : join‑keys to connect with ball_by_ball  
• player."player_id" : joins to striker to obtain the name  
• player."player_name" : human‑readable name of the striker  
• player_match."player_id", "match_id", "team_id" : lets us know for which side the striker was playing in that match (optional)  
• team."team_id", team."name" : readable team name (optional)

Main filter / condition that will finally be applied  
HAVING SUM(batsman_scored.runs_scored) > 50    -- keep only (match_id, striker) pairs where the striker scored >50

Below are ten step‑by‑step exploration queries (each limited to 20 rows) that go from simple inspection through to the final average.  
All table / column names are wrapped in double quotes to stay SQLite‑safe.

```sql
-- 1. Distinct run values that appear in batsman_scored (quick look at the metric we sum)
SELECT DISTINCT "runs_scored"
FROM "batsman_scored"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Distinct striker ids and their names seen in ball_by_ball
SELECT DISTINCT bb."striker" AS "player_id",
       p."player_name"
FROM "ball_by_ball" AS bb
JOIN "player" AS p
  ON p."player_id" = bb."striker"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Verify the join between ball_by_ball and batsman_scored for a few deliveries
SELECT bb."match_id",
       bb."over_id",
       bb."ball_id",
       bb."striker",
       bs."runs_scored"
FROM "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
JOIN "batsman_scored" AS bs
  ON bb."match_id"   = bs."match_id"
 AND bb."over_id"    = bs."over_id"
 AND bb."ball_id"    = bs."ball_id"
 AND bb."innings_no" = bs."innings_no"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Total runs per (match, striker) for a small sample
SELECT bb."match_id",
       bb."striker" AS "player_id",
       SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
FROM "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
JOIN "batsman_scored" AS bs
  ON bb."match_id"   = bs."match_id"
 AND bb."over_id"    = bs."over_id"
 AND bb."ball_id"    = bs."ball_id"
 AND bb."innings_no" = bs."innings_no"
GROUP BY bb."match_id", bb."striker"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Identify instances where a striker scored more than 50 in a match
SELECT *
FROM (
  SELECT bb."match_id",
         bb."striker" AS "player_id",
         SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
  FROM "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
  JOIN "batsman_scored" AS bs
    ON bb."match_id"   = bs."match_id"
   AND bb."over_id"    = bs."over_id"
   AND bb."ball_id"    = bs."ball_id"
   AND bb."innings_no" = bs."innings_no"
  GROUP BY bb."match_id", bb."striker"
) 
WHERE "total_runs" > 50
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Same list but with the batsman's name
SELECT sub."match_id",
       p."player_name",
       sub."total_runs"
FROM (
  SELECT bb."match_id",
         bb."striker" AS "player_id",
         SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
  FROM "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
  JOIN "batsman_scored" AS bs
    ON bb."match_id"   = bs."match_id"
   AND bb."over_id"    = bs."over_id"
   AND bb."ball_id"    = bs."ball_id"
   AND bb."innings_no" = bs."innings_no"
  GROUP BY bb."match_id", bb."striker"
) AS sub
JOIN "player" AS p
  ON p."player_id" = sub."player_id"
WHERE sub."total_runs" > 50
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. How many times has any batsman made 50+ in the data set?
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "times_scored_50_plus"
FROM (
  SELECT bb."match_id",
         bb."striker" AS "player_id",
         SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
  FROM "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
  JOIN "batsman_scored" AS bs
    ON bb."match_id"   = bs."match_id"
   AND bb."over_id"    = bs."over_id"
   AND bb."ball_id"    = bs."ball_id"
   AND bb."innings_no" = bs."innings_no"
  GROUP BY bb."match_id", bb."striker"
  HAVING SUM(bs."runs_scored") > 50
);
```

```sql
-- 8. Average runs scored by those 50+ knocks (core answer)
SELECT AVG("total_runs") AS "average_runs_above_50"
FROM (
  SELECT bb."match_id",
         bb."striker" AS "player_id",
         SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
  FROM "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
  JOIN "batsman_scored" AS bs
    ON bb."match_id"   = bs."match_id"
   AND bb."over_id"    = bs."over_id"
   AND bb."ball_id"    = bs."ball_id"
   AND bb."innings_no" = bs."innings_no"
  GROUP BY bb."match_id", bb."striker"
  HAVING SUM(bs."runs_scored") > 50
);
```

```sql
-- 9. Display the 50+ knocks together with the team they were scored for
SELECT sub."match_id",
       t."name"       AS "team_name",
       p."player_name",
       sub."total_runs"
FROM (
  SELECT bb."match_id",
         bb."striker" AS "player_id",
         SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
  FROM "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
  JOIN "batsman_scored" AS bs
    ON bb."match_id"   = bs."match_id"
   AND bb."over_id"    = bs."over_id"
   AND bb."ball_id"    = bs."ball_id"
   AND bb."innings_no" = bs."innings_no"
  GROUP BY bb."match_id", bb."striker"
  HAVING SUM(bs."runs_scored") > 50
) AS sub
JOIN "player_match" AS pm
  ON pm."match_id" = sub."match_id"
 AND pm."player_id" = sub."player_id"
JOIN "team" AS t
  ON t."team_id" = pm."team_id"
JOIN "player" AS p
  ON p."player_id" = sub."player_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Same average as query 8 but expressed through a CTE (alternative syntax)
WITH totals AS (
  SELECT bb."match_id",
         bb."striker" AS "player_id",
         SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
  FROM "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
  JOIN "batsman_scored" AS bs
    ON bb."match_id"   = bs."match_id"
   AND bb."over_id"    = bs."over_id"
   AND bb."ball_id"    = bs."ball_id"
   AND bb."innings_no" = bs."innings_no"
  GROUP BY bb."match_id", bb."striker"
)
SELECT AVG("total_runs") AS "average_50_plus_runs"
FROM totals
WHERE "total_runs" > 50;
```
